4 hr @ 140.00/hr ... 196.00.\" Operation, hours, and rate are shown. |\n| 3 | Check | \"Shop supplies ... 10.00.\" This is a flat fee with no contents stated (F-2). |\n| 4 | Standard | \"Sales tax 7.25% ... 21.39.\" Rate is stated and the arithmetic checks. |\n\n## Questions to ask\n1. **What did the inspection find that points to the rear shoes as the cause of the grinding, and were the drums and hardware checked too?** A good answer names a specific finding, such as measured lining thickness, visible wear, or damage, and says whether the rest of the rear brake assembly was looked at.\n2. **What does the $10 shop supplies fee cover?** A good answer lists the consumables or explains how the flat amount is set.\n3. **Is the 1.4 hours a book-time figure from a labor guide, and does it include any diagnosis?** A good answer names the guide or the basis and says whether the diagnosis is billed separately or included.\n4. **Is the $89 shoe part a specific brand or grade (OEM, aftermarket, or other), and is there a core charge or return requirement?** A good answer names the brand tier and states whether any money comes back.\n5. **Until what date is this estimate valid, and where is my signed authorization recorded?** A good answer gives a date and shows you the authorization line before any work starts.\n\n## Decision\nI'm not approving, declining, or recommending anything here. That decision is yours. The habit that helps most right now is documentation: photograph the estimate before you sign anything, write down what the service advisor tells you and their name, and keep every receipt and paper you're given. If the shop says anything verbally that isn't on the paper, note it on the paper with the date.\n\n## Needs confirmation\n[NOT SHOWN: diagnosis or inspection findings behind the rear-shoe work]\n[NOT SHOWN: shoe brand or grade, and any core charge]\n[NOT SHOWN: contents of the $10 shop supplies fee]\n[NOT SHOWN: source of the 1.4-hour book time]\n[NOT SHOWN: estimate validity date]\n[NOT SHOWN: customer authorization line]","refusal":null,"reasoning":null,"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2927,"completion_tokens":3176,"total_tokens":6103,"cost":0.0018807,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.0018807,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.0002927,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.001588},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1796,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}